                <pb facs="0779" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.55/177a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Rumania</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-06-06T14:00:00-04:00">June 6, 1939—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. United Press despatch of May 22 states that over 700 Vienna Jews sailed from
                    Constanza for an unknown destination on the S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alexander</hi> or <hi rendition="#italic">Alexandria</hi>. Please
                    ascertain, if possible, destination of this boat.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
